    "details": {
      "isComplex": true,
      "level": {
        "value": 5
      },
      "disable": "<p>@Check[type:arcana|dc:17|name:To Identify Box as Being Necromantic |traits:complex,haunt] (expert)To Identify Box as Being Necromantic,</p>\n<p>@Check[type:arcana|dc:20|name:To Dispel|traits:complex,haunt] (expert) Twice To Dispel,</p>\n<p>@Check[type:religion|dc:23|name: To Dispel|traits:complex,haunt] (expert) Twice To Dispel,</p>\n<p>@Check[type:nature|dc:23|name: To Dispel|traits:complex,haunt] (expert) Twice To Dispel,</p>\n<p>@Check[type:occultism|dc:23|name: To Dispel|traits:complex,haunt] (expert) Twice To Dispel,</p>\n<p>@Check[type:perception|dc:17|name:To Notice Humanoid Shape In Fungus|traits:complex,haunt] To Notice Humanoid Shape In Fungus</p>\n<p>@Check[type:perception|dc:21|name:To Notice Rattling Shards of the Phylactery|traits:complex,haunt] To Notice Rattling Shards of the Phylactery</p>",
      "description": "<p>You see a humanoid shape cast on the cavern wall, outlined among the rocks and odd fungus growing there. With a flash of insight, you realize the cavern is trying to steal your shadow. You must eat the fungus to reclaim your shadow!</p>",
      "reset": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Though tho fungus can be temporarily disabled by fire or application of holy water, it will rsset in 24 hours if not disabled via a counteract check against a level 3 spell effect from dispel magic or by succeeding in two DC23 expert checks in a row in Religion, Oocultism, Nature or Arcana.</p>",
      "routine": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Vorel's Compulsion <span class=\"pf2-icon\">R</span></strong> (Enchantment, Mental] <strong>Trlgger</strong> Haunted creature gets within 5 foot of the fungus. Creature must make a @Check[type:will|dc:23] or he is compelled to eat the fungus to reclaim his own shadow.&nbsp;</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Festering Haunt: </strong>This haunt only effects those haunted by Vorel Foxgovs and his painful death by a thousand necromantic diseases. If no creatures in a group are haunted by Vorel Foxglove, this haunt may tangot any creatire in a group.</p>"
    },
